WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.305
Roof inspections can document surface condition, drainage, penetrations, flashing, debris,

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:06.240
and storm effects.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.205
Thermal patterns may support moisture or insulation screening under suitable conditions,

00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:14.200
but roofing material, sun, weather, and indoor conditions create alternatives.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.535
Bridge and structural observation can document accessible surfaces, joints, bearings,

00:00:18.535 --> 00:00:22.190
drainage, staining, spalling-like features, deformation indicators,

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:23.520
and surrounding access.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.925
Structural significance requires qualified engineering review and often hands-on methods.

00:00:27.925 --> 00:00:31.247
Utility and tower inspections may examine components, connections,

00:00:31.247 --> 00:00:33.610
corrosion-like features, vegetation proximity,

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:36.280
or visible damage from a safe authorized distance.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.215
Power, radio-frequency, wind, access,

00:00:38.215 --> 00:00:41.960
and critical-infrastructure controls require specialist coordination.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.350
Solar-array review combines visible condition with thermal screening where appropriate.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:50.480
Load, irradiance, wind, angle, cleanliness, reflections, and array design affect patterns.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.330
Electrical interpretation and corrective action belong to qualified personnel.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:59.365
Pipeline, road, rail, water, and industrial-corridor observation can document erosion,

00:00:59.365 --> 00:01:03.887
encroachment, surface change, leakage indicators, obstructions, or storm impact.

00:01:03.887 --> 00:01:07.490
Corridor operations require careful airspace, access, traffic, communication,

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:09.080
and privacy planning.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:11.350
Damage assessment can accelerate situational awareness,

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.650
but urgent conditions do not remove authorization or safety requirements.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:19.070
Use specialists when findings affect structural, electrical, process, environmental, fire,

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:20.760
or life-safety decisions.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.586
Some defects remain inaccessible to aerial imagery.

00:01:23.586 --> 00:01:27.040
Internal corrosion, hidden connections, subsurface damage, material strength,

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.395
and many electrical conditions require hands-on, instrumented, or destructive methods.

00:01:31.395 --> 00:01:32.860
Report that boundary explicitly.
